From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:40:59 +0100
Subject: media: i2c: imx214: keep the reset GPIO optional

The reset GPIO handling added for the Radxa camera made the GPIO
mandatory, so boards that only describe enable-gpios no longer probe.
Request it as optional, since gpiod calls ignore a NULL descriptor.

Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx214.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx214.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx214.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx214.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx214.c
@@ -1416,7 +1416,7 @@ static int imx214_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to get regulators\n");
 
-	imx214->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
+	imx214->reset_gpio = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "reset", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
 	if (IS_ERR(imx214->reset_gpio))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(imx214->reset_gpio),
 				     "failed to get reset gpio\n");
-- 
Armbian

